👋 Welcome, everyone!

Today we're going to learn how computers understand our instructions using a language called Python.

Think of Python as a language that helps us talk to computers. Just like we use English to talk to people, we use Python to tell computers what to do.

On this platform, we can:

Write Python code
Run our programs instantly
See the output of our code
Create games, quizzes, calculators, and much more
Quick Activity

Ask:

"If you had a robot at home, what instructions would you give it?"

Let students answer things like:

Bring me water
Clean my room
Dance

Then explain:

"A computer is like a robot. It only does exactly what we tell it to do. The step-by-step instructions we give are called an algorithm."

Mini Algorithm Activity

Make a Sandwich 🥪

Start
Take two slices of bread
Add jam
Close the sandwich
Eat
Stop

Then ask:

"What happens if we forget step 3?"

This helps them understand why computers need clear instructions.
